1
00:02:30,059 --> 00:02:35,059
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,059 --> 00:02:40,059
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,059 --> 00:02:44,059
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:49,059
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,059 --> 00:02:52,059
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,059 --> 00:02:55,059
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,059 --> 00:02:58,059
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,059 --> 00:03:01,059
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:01,059 --> 00:03:04,059
This is exciting!

10
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:07,059
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,059 --> 00:03:11,059
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,059 --> 00:03:15,059
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,059 --> 00:03:24,059
Luffy has returned to Marineford with Rayleigh and Jinbei at his side.

14
00:03:24,059 --> 00:03:27,059
For what reason did they go back?

15
00:03:27,059 --> 00:03:30,059
And why did Luffy ring the Oxbell?

16
00:03:36,059 --> 00:03:38,059
With hopes it will reach my friends!

17
00:03:38,059 --> 00:03:40,059
Big news spreading fast!

18
00:03:40,059 --> 00:03:49,059
On a certain island along the Grand Line...

19
00:03:49,059 --> 00:03:55,059
Times have been rough since you got locked up.

20
00:03:55,059 --> 00:03:59,059
We couldn't even sleep at night, but we knew we had to get you back somehow.

21
00:03:59,059 --> 00:04:04,059
We sailed all over in search of you, surviving countless hardships along the way.

22
00:04:04,059 --> 00:04:06,059
But then...

23
00:04:06,059 --> 00:04:09,059
We saw our very own Captain, a hero in the newspaper!

24
00:04:13,059 --> 00:04:15,059
Welcome back!

25
00:04:15,059 --> 00:04:16,059
Finally!

26
00:04:19,059 --> 00:04:21,059
We're with you till the end.

27
00:04:21,059 --> 00:04:23,059
A little wait like that is nothing.

28
00:04:23,059 --> 00:04:27,059
Our very own Captain Buggy leading us into the New World!

29
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:31,059
I didn't know you guys cared about me so much!

30
00:04:32,059 --> 00:04:34,059
I missed all of you too!

31
00:04:34,059 --> 00:04:35,059
Captain!

32
00:04:42,059 --> 00:04:44,059
Bunch of liars.

33
00:04:45,059 --> 00:04:47,059
I seem to recall you giving up on him.

34
00:04:47,059 --> 00:05:00,059
Welcome to the crew, fellas!

35
00:05:02,059 --> 00:05:06,059
I'm the first mate of the Buggy Pirates, Beast Tamer Moji!

36
00:05:06,059 --> 00:05:08,059
Brother Moji!

37
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:12,059
And I'm the Chief of Staff, Kabaji!

38
00:05:12,059 --> 00:05:14,059
Brother Kabaji!

39
00:05:14,059 --> 00:05:16,059
And this here's my buddy!

40
00:05:16,059 --> 00:05:18,059
The one and only Richie!

41
00:05:20,059 --> 00:05:21,059
Richie!

42
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:27,059
Impressive.

43
00:05:27,059 --> 00:05:30,059
Looks like what the paper said about your new followers turned out to be true.

44
00:05:30,059 --> 00:05:35,059
Though I'm almost afraid to ask how you got so many infamous criminals to follow you.

45
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:37,059
Give me some credit.

46
00:05:38,059 --> 00:05:41,059
Clearly when it comes to scoundrels, I'm a natural born leader.

47
00:05:41,059 --> 00:05:46,059
Oh, by the way, I picked up a little something on my trip that you might find interesting.

48
00:05:46,059 --> 00:05:47,059
Huh?

49
00:05:48,059 --> 00:05:49,059
Ta-da!

50
00:05:50,059 --> 00:05:51,059
It can't be!

51
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,059
Very nice!

52
00:05:53,059 --> 00:05:55,059
You finally found Captain John's armband, huh?

53
00:05:56,059 --> 00:05:57,059
Sure did!

54
00:05:57,059 --> 00:05:58,059
Don't leave me in suspense!

55
00:05:58,059 --> 00:06:00,059
How did you get your hands on this?

56
00:06:01,059 --> 00:06:04,059
That idiot's straw hat gave it to me without a second thought!

57
00:06:05,059 --> 00:06:09,059
Everything's coming up, Flashy! The wind is blowing my way!

58
00:06:10,059 --> 00:06:13,059
Could it be Buggy was meant to be king of the pirates?

59
00:06:14,059 --> 00:06:18,059
Oh, speaking of straw hat, he's still making a name for himself after the war.

60
00:06:19,059 --> 00:06:20,059
Huh?

61
00:06:21,059 --> 00:06:22,059
You didn't know?

62
00:06:22,059 --> 00:06:24,059
He caused quite a stir returning to Marineford.

63
00:06:24,059 --> 00:06:25,059
You're kidding me!

64
00:06:26,059 --> 00:06:28,059
He was barely alive when I last saw him.

65
00:06:29,059 --> 00:06:30,059
And now this?

66
00:06:31,059 --> 00:06:32,059
Uh, let's see.

67
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:35,059
First son of the sea, Jinbei, teams up with straw hat.

68
00:06:36,059 --> 00:06:38,059
Dark King Rayleigh joins them.

69
00:06:39,059 --> 00:06:40,059
Rayleigh?

70
00:06:41,059 --> 00:06:42,059
Ah!

71
00:06:42,059 --> 00:06:43,059
This is a joke, right?

72
00:06:43,059 --> 00:06:45,059
Since when did Rayleigh get involved with straw hats?

73
00:06:45,059 --> 00:06:50,059
This just keeps on getting messier.

74
00:06:51,059 --> 00:06:53,059
I can't wrap my head around this at all!

75
00:06:54,059 --> 00:06:55,059
Wait a sec.

76
00:06:56,059 --> 00:06:58,059
If I'm remembering it correctly,

77
00:06:58,059 --> 00:07:01,059
Straw Hat's pop is the revolutionary dragon.

78
00:07:01,059 --> 00:07:03,059
On top of that, his grandpa's garb.

79
00:07:04,059 --> 00:07:05,059
It could only mean one thing.

80
00:07:06,059 --> 00:07:09,059
Really, must be Straw Hat's long-lost uncle!

81
00:07:10,059 --> 00:07:11,059
Hey, Buggy!

82
00:07:11,059 --> 00:07:16,059
A carrier bat brought a message for you from the government.

83
00:07:17,059 --> 00:07:18,059
How did they find me?

84
00:07:19,059 --> 00:07:20,059
Did someone rat me out?

85
00:07:20,059 --> 00:07:23,059
The Navy must be trying to strike me down before I'm too strong!

86
00:07:24,059 --> 00:07:26,059
Which means the message is my final warning.

87
00:07:28,059 --> 00:07:29,059
Hey!

88
00:07:29,059 --> 00:07:30,059
Give me that letter!

89
00:07:32,059 --> 00:07:33,059
It can't be!

90
00:07:35,059 --> 00:07:36,059
This is simply unbelievable!

91
00:07:37,059 --> 00:07:38,059
Hey, that's from me!

92
00:07:38,059 --> 00:07:39,059
Stop it!

93
00:07:40,059 --> 00:07:44,059
Meanwhile, at the Saba Odi Archipelago, along the Grand Line,

94
00:07:45,059 --> 00:07:47,059
the Thousand Sunny waits for its crew,

95
00:07:48,059 --> 00:07:50,059
anchored at Grove Number 44.

96
00:07:51,059 --> 00:07:54,059
Either you hand over the ship, or we bust your faces in!

97
00:07:55,059 --> 00:07:56,059
You can't fool us!

98
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:59,059
We know it belongs to Straw Hat, and we know he's Dragon's son!

99
00:08:00,059 --> 00:08:02,059
The Navy's bound to pay good money for it,

100
00:08:02,059 --> 00:08:04,059
so walk away and we won't hurt ya!

101
00:08:04,059 --> 00:08:09,059
Since you and I are in the same line of work,

102
00:08:09,059 --> 00:08:12,059
give it up now and you'll get a cut of the profit!

103
00:08:12,059 --> 00:08:13,059
Easy, right?

104
00:08:14,059 --> 00:08:16,059
How about it, Flying Fish Riders?

105
00:08:17,059 --> 00:08:18,059
Hmm.

106
00:08:18,059 --> 00:08:19,059
Hmm.

107
00:08:25,059 --> 00:08:26,059
What? I'm handsome?

108
00:08:27,059 --> 00:08:28,059
I didn't say that, weirdo!

109
00:08:28,059 --> 00:08:29,059
We're true, it's played around!

110
00:08:31,059 --> 00:08:33,059
You punks ain't getting nothing from me!

111
00:08:33,059 --> 00:08:34,059
Ugh!

112
00:08:42,059 --> 00:08:43,059
Ugh!

113
00:08:43,059 --> 00:08:44,059
Enough of this!

114
00:08:49,059 --> 00:08:50,059
Huh?

115
00:08:50,059 --> 00:08:51,059
Listen up, you losers!

116
00:08:51,059 --> 00:08:56,059
I, the very handsome Duval, refuse to let a bunch of ugly fools like you become popular!

117
00:08:57,059 --> 00:08:59,059
Uh, I mean, try to steal our friend's ship on my watch!

118
00:09:00,059 --> 00:09:01,059
Stay unpopular!

119
00:09:02,059 --> 00:09:04,059
Well, as long as he protects the ship, we're okay!

120
00:09:05,059 --> 00:09:09,059
You won't touch this ship as long as I live, and before I die, I'm gonna touch a girl!

121
00:09:10,059 --> 00:09:11,059
I mean, if you touch it, you're gonna die!

122
00:09:12,059 --> 00:09:13,059
The ship, I mean, not the girl!

123
00:09:14,059 --> 00:09:16,059
The bottom line is, you're not getting near the Sunny,

124
00:09:16,059 --> 00:09:17,059
but if you want to fight, come and get it!

125
00:09:18,059 --> 00:09:19,059
Yeah, tough guy!

126
00:09:21,059 --> 00:09:22,059
Come on! Let's book it!

127
00:09:24,059 --> 00:09:25,059
Wow, Duval! Nice one!

128
00:09:27,059 --> 00:09:30,059
The girls won't leave me alone because I'm so handsome!

129
00:09:32,059 --> 00:09:34,059
Thanks for the support! I love you two!

130
00:09:35,059 --> 00:09:38,059
The Mermaid Cafe should obviously be the first stop, don't you think?

131
00:09:39,059 --> 00:09:40,059
It's so in style!

132
00:09:41,059 --> 00:09:45,059
Nah, once they get back, I'm sure the first place they'll want to see is the Fishman Karate Training Hall!

133
00:09:46,059 --> 00:09:49,059
Wait a minute! I already promised Brooke I'd introduce him to the Mermaid Princess!

134
00:09:49,059 --> 00:09:52,059
Hey, boss! It's like she doesn't even know you're there!

135
00:09:52,059 --> 00:09:54,059
I can wait! That's cool!

136
00:09:55,059 --> 00:09:59,059
Oh, I almost forgot to ask! The Straw Hats can use their Vivre cards to get back here, right?

137
00:10:00,059 --> 00:10:03,059
Now that we all know Luffy Toon's alive, they should be here soon!

138
00:10:03,059 --> 00:10:11,059
Maybe. If they're far away, it might take them a while, but Ray found Monkey easy enough with his Vivre card.

139
00:10:14,059 --> 00:10:17,059
Until then, we have to protect this ship.

140
00:10:17,059 --> 00:10:21,059
Don't you worry, because we're here to do exactly that!

141
00:10:22,059 --> 00:10:26,059
Whether it's the Navy or somebody else, nobody's gonna take the ship!

142
00:10:27,059 --> 00:10:30,059
So far, you're doing great!

143
00:10:30,059 --> 00:10:36,059
Hey, Duvall! We've got a huge problem! Kuma's heading this way!

144
00:10:37,059 --> 00:10:39,059
Kuma? Do I know a Kuma?

145
00:10:40,059 --> 00:10:41,059
Oh, right!

146
00:10:41,059 --> 00:10:42,059
Oh, right!

147
00:10:49,059 --> 00:10:51,059
It's the Warlord! Bartholomew Kuma!

148
00:10:51,059 --> 00:10:52,059
Hey, Kuma!

149
00:11:08,059 --> 00:11:09,059
Relax, everyone.

150
00:11:10,059 --> 00:11:13,059
That man, he came to speak with Ray before.

151
00:11:14,059 --> 00:11:18,059
So tell me, Kuma, whose side are you on?

152
00:11:21,059 --> 00:11:30,059
Meanwhile, on Sandy Island, part of Alabasta Kingdom on the Grand Line,

153
00:11:32,059 --> 00:11:34,059
the capital city, Alubarna.

154
00:11:38,059 --> 00:11:39,059
What happened to the pirates?

155
00:11:40,059 --> 00:11:43,059
We chased them away. The city is virtually undamaged.

156
00:11:44,059 --> 00:11:45,059
I see. Good job.

157
00:11:46,059 --> 00:11:48,059
We're strengthening security across the country.

158
00:11:48,059 --> 00:11:52,059
Ever since Whitebeard's death, pirates around the world are more active.

159
00:11:53,059 --> 00:11:54,059
Our region is no exception.

160
00:11:55,059 --> 00:11:56,059
We have to be careful for the time being.

161
00:11:57,059 --> 00:12:01,059
If only all pirates were like Straw Hat Luffy and his crew.

162
00:12:02,059 --> 00:12:04,059
But such is not the case.

163
00:12:05,059 --> 00:12:08,059
Speaking of Luffy, have you read today's newspaper?

164
00:12:09,059 --> 00:12:10,059
Yes, I did.

165
00:12:10,059 --> 00:12:11,059
Whoa!

166
00:12:12,059 --> 00:12:15,059
Vivi was ecstatic when she read about Luffy and the others!

167
00:12:16,059 --> 00:12:17,059
Huh. Of course she was.

168
00:12:18,059 --> 00:12:19,059
But...

169
00:12:23,059 --> 00:12:24,059
Karu!

170
00:12:25,059 --> 00:12:27,059
Take a look at this!

171
00:12:28,059 --> 00:12:31,059
Thank goodness! Luffy is still alive!

172
00:12:31,059 --> 00:12:35,059
I'm so glad. I just knew he'd be okay.

173
00:12:36,059 --> 00:12:37,059
Huh? What?

174
00:12:40,059 --> 00:12:44,059
Within a single moment, her entire demeanor changed and all of her joy suddenly vanished.

175
00:12:45,059 --> 00:12:48,059
She took the newspaper and ran towards her room.

176
00:12:48,059 --> 00:12:54,059
Huh. What's that on Luffy's arm?

177
00:12:55,059 --> 00:12:57,059
Numbers? Is it a code?

178
00:12:58,059 --> 00:13:00,059
Well, it's not a tattoo, right?

179
00:13:01,059 --> 00:13:04,059
That doesn't really seem like Luffy's style, does it?

180
00:13:04,059 --> 00:13:16,059
Meanwhile, in another city, in another country, along the Grand Line...

181
00:13:21,059 --> 00:13:24,059
Whoa! Hey! What's a hardcore pirate like him doing on our island?

182
00:13:25,059 --> 00:13:26,059
Hush! He can hear you!

183
00:13:27,059 --> 00:13:29,059
It's only been three weeks since the war.

184
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:34,059
They were lucky to escape death at Marineford.

185
00:13:37,059 --> 00:13:39,059
What the hell would bring them back there?

186
00:13:40,059 --> 00:13:42,059
Straw Hat's probably cooking up some plan.

187
00:13:43,059 --> 00:13:44,059
Either that or he's just crazy.

188
00:13:45,059 --> 00:13:47,059
That sounds about right.

189
00:13:48,059 --> 00:13:50,059
He was badly injured in the fight, though.

190
00:13:51,059 --> 00:13:54,059
Takes someone pretty special to get back on their feet so quickly.

191
00:13:55,059 --> 00:13:58,059
You saying I'm slower than Straw Hat?

192
00:13:58,059 --> 00:14:00,059
Trying to challenge your old boss?

193
00:14:02,059 --> 00:14:04,059
I'm done resting, don't worry.

194
00:14:05,059 --> 00:14:07,059
There's no point in staying here any longer.

195
00:14:08,059 --> 00:14:10,059
It's time to set out for the new world.

196
00:14:11,059 --> 00:14:13,059
Are you coming, Daz?

197
00:14:15,059 --> 00:14:16,059
Of course I am.

198
00:14:16,059 --> 00:14:18,059
The news of Luffy's latest exploits, as well as his return to World War II.

199
00:14:18,059 --> 00:14:19,059
The news of Luffy's latest exploits, as well as his return to World War II.

200
00:14:19,059 --> 00:14:22,059
The news of Luffy's latest exploits, as well as his return to Marineford, quickly spread to each crew member's home.

201
00:14:22,059 --> 00:14:23,059
The news of Luffy's latest exploits, as well as his return to Marineford, quickly spread to each crew member's home.

202
00:14:23,059 --> 00:14:36,059
The news of Luffy's latest exploits, as well as his return to Marineford, quickly spread to each crew member's hometown.

203
00:14:36,059 --> 00:14:49,059
The news of Luffy's latest exploits, as well as Luffy's latest exploits, as well as his return to Marineford, quickly spread to each crew member's hometown.

204
00:14:49,059 --> 00:15:03,059
Get a load of this, Ace!

205
00:15:04,059 --> 00:15:07,059
You saved your little brother's life! Luffy is alive!

206
00:15:10,059 --> 00:15:16,059
Rest in peace, you brat!

207
00:15:19,059 --> 00:15:25,059
Meanwhile, on the Grand Line...

208
00:15:26,059 --> 00:15:30,059
Really sorry you had to go so far out of your way.

209
00:15:30,059 --> 00:15:33,059
It's nothing. We're pretty used to being away from home.

210
00:15:33,059 --> 00:15:34,059
Um, what are you doing?

211
00:15:34,059 --> 00:15:37,059
Huh? We're making sure that you're resting properly, of course!

212
00:15:37,059 --> 00:15:40,059
Orders from the Snake Princess herself!

213
00:15:40,059 --> 00:15:44,059
But she couldn't stay, because she collapsed from a severe case of heart cluttering.

214
00:15:44,059 --> 00:15:48,059
So here we are, keeping a close eye on you.

215
00:15:48,059 --> 00:15:54,059
I hope they get the message, wherever they are.

216
00:15:54,059 --> 00:16:01,059
They'll understand if they see the article. Obviously, this isn't something you would do on a whim.

217
00:16:01,059 --> 00:16:02,059
Would you stop, please?

218
00:16:02,059 --> 00:16:13,059
That said, your swordsman can be a bit daft. Still, I think you'll figure it out somehow. They are your crew, after all. If anyone can understand you, it's them.

219
00:16:13,059 --> 00:16:19,059
Above the Grand Line, high in the air...

220
00:16:20,059 --> 00:16:30,059
I got it, Luffy! Don't worry! I'm changing plans, Dad! Yeah! Okay! Okay!

221
00:16:30,059 --> 00:16:37,059
On the giant bridge, reaching across the East Blue...

222
00:16:37,059 --> 00:16:42,059
So that's it. Very well, then.

223
00:16:42,059 --> 00:16:45,059
Something in the paper again? Good news, I hope.

224
00:16:45,059 --> 00:16:51,059
Interesting as always, Luffy.

225
00:16:51,059 --> 00:17:00,059
And in Kamabaka Kingdom...

226
00:17:00,059 --> 00:17:06,059
Roger that, Captain.

227
00:17:06,059 --> 00:17:08,059
What's going on?

228
00:17:08,059 --> 00:17:15,059
The Bowen Islands.

229
00:17:15,059 --> 00:17:26,059
I gotta find a way off! I gotta find a way off this island!

230
00:17:26,059 --> 00:17:30,059
Ouch! Ouch! I'm so sick of this!

231
00:17:30,059 --> 00:17:45,059
Get away from me! I don't care what you have to say!

232
00:17:45,059 --> 00:17:50,059
One way or another, I'm gonna get to Luffy even if it kills me!

233
00:17:50,059 --> 00:17:54,059
Look at that! I think I made it! Is that the shore?!

234
00:17:54,059 --> 00:17:56,059
You've barely gone 50 feet.

235
00:17:56,059 --> 00:17:58,059
No!

236
00:17:58,059 --> 00:18:04,059
Damn it! Why does everything here have to be so delicious?!

237
00:18:04,059 --> 00:18:06,059
I'm still hungry!

238
00:18:06,059 --> 00:18:10,059
Stop it, Usoppin! You're already dangerously obese-y!

239
00:18:10,059 --> 00:18:12,059
Don't give in to the island's trap!

240
00:18:12,059 --> 00:18:15,059
Can't you see I'm busy?!

241
00:18:15,059 --> 00:18:18,059
Huh? Huh?

242
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:24,059
I've got it!

243
00:18:24,059 --> 00:18:26,059
What is it this time, Usoppin?

244
00:18:26,059 --> 00:18:28,059
Yes, Luffy! Yes!

245
00:18:32,059 --> 00:18:34,059
The Sky Island with area.

246
00:18:40,059 --> 00:18:42,059
Hey, hey, hey, hey, young lady!

247
00:18:42,059 --> 00:18:43,059
Where are you running off to?

248
00:18:43,059 --> 00:18:44,059
Not now!

249
00:18:44,059 --> 00:18:45,059
Not now!

250
00:18:45,059 --> 00:18:50,059
Well, I thought you should know that they closed the balloon terminal after you tried to escape!

251
00:18:50,059 --> 00:18:53,059
And since the island's so small, there's nowhere to run!

252
00:18:53,059 --> 00:18:56,059
Well, you better come up with something quick then! I have to get away from here!

253
